! Causal Island — Ontological Law

<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

`island-protocol.ts` owns the ontological law that names where one island ends and
another begins, the per-bag ''ACCESS'' axis (a MODEL mirroring Keyhive's native
Access enum), and the edge-island federation scaffolding. The boundary law sits
above any vessel implementation; every vessel honors it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/no-global-now`>>

!! No Global Now

Fuller-Zelenka: the Universe holds no simultaneously-apprehended present. A node
never grasps the full state of a distributed system "at once" — it holds a
snapshot of what it has synchronized so far. This topology ''defines'' the
system; it names no limitation the system suffers.

Simultaneously apprehended: the local Automerge doc snapshot, right now.
Non-simultaneously apprehended: every other peer's state (seen at last sync),
every other reachable Realm, every un-hydrated tiddler, every active-meme
instance with its own event horizon.

''Law:'' any boundary across which causality cannot stand guaranteed-simultaneous
marks a ''causal island boundary''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/four-tiers`>>

!! Four Tiers (inner → outer)

| Tier | Boundary | Status |
|---|---|---|
| ''0'' | Active memes (kumu / UEFN device instances) | MAY become islands — own event horizon, params, trigger surface; promotion optional, correction local |
| ''1'' | Memes inside a wiki (within the local doc window) | Simultaneously apprehended; peer state of the same doc remains non-simultaneous |
| ''2'' | Automerge Realms (other docs reachable from this one) | Always non-simultaneous |
| ''3'' | Lares nodes (federation edge) | A pranala/peer connection between nodes MUST count as an island boundary |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/substrate-not-sovereignty`>>

!! Share Substrate, Not Sovereignty (load-bearing)

A causal island earns its identity from ''a separate log + no shared now'' — never
from separate silicon. Co-location collapses nothing by itself: many sovereign
vessels MAY run on one machine. The smell lives one layer down — whether they
share ''mutable state'' or merely a ''substrate''.

| Substrate — MAY co-hold | Sovereignty — MUST stay separate |
|---|---|
| the machine, the disk device | the Automerge ''replica'' (each peer holds its own) |
| a ''relay'' peer (carries sync, holds no authority) | the ''heap / process'' (no shared mutable RAM) |
| the network, the loopback transport | the ''storage scope'' (own dir / own IndexedDB) |
| canon bags (read, by CRDT merge) | the ''keys + the log + the "now"'' |

''Two boundaries, both MUST hold.'' ''Vessel ↔ vessel'' reconciles via CRDT over
a transport — each vessel its own replica; the loopback WS between two local
processes counts as a real Tier-3 boundary (the V3 auth gate guards it). ''Island''
''↔ island within one vessel'' passes structured-clone messages over a MessagePort —
Worker threads never share a heap (the no-VM-on-main law,
[[project_no_vm_on_main_thread]]).

''The anti-pattern, named:'' several "vessels" behind one Repo, one heap, or one
storage dir — a distributed monolith wearing many costumes (fake sovereignty). The
tree already refuses it: the CLI carries an ephemeral in-RAM replica and syncs over
WS (it touches no daemon storage), and in-process ephemeral boot stays deferred until
contention rules around NodeFS storage land.

''Efficiency rides the role split, not a shared heap.'' Role reads as a held
Keyhive capability, not a platform (`[[feedback_isomorphism_by_composition]]`). One
''relay'' (the heavy peer) carries the canonical replica + the disk; ''leaf'' peers
(CLI, AI agent) stay thin — they hold only the bags they reach, sync from the relay,
own their keys. //Heavy peer = substrate, not authority.// So co-located peers share a
relay (infrastructure), never a replica (sovereignty).

The principle reconciles local-first
multi-peer co-location with sovereignty: one substrate may carry many sovereign
islands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/access-axis`>>

!! ACCESS Axis (Axis 1 of the authority model)

''THE AXIS IS A MODEL; THE GATE IS BINARY.'' `pull · read · edit · admin` mirrors Keyhive's own verbs
one-for-one and names how authority is TALKED ABOUT. Nothing checks it: `CapabilityAccess` is
`"read" | "admin"` (capability.ts), the live gate runs `CapabilityVerifier.verify({ access })` over
those two, and no call site in this tree narrows an action by verb.

''Naming the ladder here as a checked tier would promise a reader a gate they could then fail to find''
— and this room did exactly that, describing a typed four-level constant that exists in no source file.
A reader who trusted it would design against a gradation the substrate has never enforced. The sibling
law at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/keyhive/capability-provider`>> states the same limit from
the provider's side.

''Relay-law exception:'' `pull` does NOT imply `read`. A relay holds pull and
forwards ENCRYPTED bytes it cannot decrypt or render. Every other level implies all
levels beneath it.

The other authority dimensions live elsewhere: Axis 2 SCALE (Keyhive group
nesting), Axis 3 POWERS (host/relay/aggregate/address/moderate separation), Plane 0
ALIGNMENT (the non-monotonic lemures plane). See
`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/causal-islands`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/selected-contracts`>>

!! Two selected contracts ~ a worker's own storage scope, and typed authority evidence

Both follow from the law above (operator ruling): a parent Repo never becomes a worker's storage by
implication, and no relation borrows another relation's epoch.

!!! The daemon worker's restart contract (capability-pinned hybrid)

* ''Ordinary reads stay parent-attached.'' The daemon worker's primary Repo carries oracle, persona, catalog, crossroads and recipe documents through the parent crossing and persists none of them.
* ''Only a worker-owned document recovers from the worker's own storage.'' The manifest names one owned document, its own transferred port and its own physical root (`ownedDocument`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts`); the owned Repo admits that document alone. The daemon document stands as the first owned scope, on node and in the browser.
* ''A refusal keeps its name'': `worker-parent-required`, `document-not-resident`, `storage-corrupt`, `storage-quota`, `replay-incomplete`, `peer-required`. No process turns one into a successful empty document or a silent re-fetch. A CRDT conflict keeps both heads and goes to the operator's Talk Story.
* ''Pin state names itself.'' Residency stays an Island Pool fact, with pinning apart from `wela` and `anu` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/residency-tiers`>>); a compaction cut never reads as an authority epoch (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/compaction-handlers`>>).
* ''Owed'': a general document pin with a real physical storage boundary, its entry in the residency inventory, and the corrupt and quota refusals under test. A label, a post-save filter or bag hotness never stands in for that boundary.

!!! Typed authority evidence, per relation

* ''No mesh-wide epoch exists.'' The lease frontier, the charter lineage, PersonaGroup or realm membership, the CGKA epoch and the compaction cut stay separate values (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/epoch-binding-surfaces`>>).
* ''Every relation tells five states apart'' before it applies its own policy (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/authority-verdict.ts`): `checked-valid`, the verifier holds and walks the named witness; `unavailable`, it lacks the witness or the local material, which proves no revocation; `stale`, a newer causal head stands known; `malformed`, a byte, signature, predecessor, audience or resource check fails; `revoked`, an explicit kapae or later authority state shadows the grant.
* ''A mutation gate rejects `malformed` and `revoked`, and answers `stale` or `unavailable` with its named refusal or a pending receipt.'' A stale Handle may render as a labelled observation alone. Daemon proof replay stays scoped to its connection, and a restart takes a fresh handshake. Contract and Cabal mutation each require their own current accepted frontier.
* ''No gate turns `unavailable` into `checked-valid`'' by reading wall time or by inferring a realm epoch.
* ''A relation's proof names'' its resource, relation, owner, audience, capability, witness kind, causal head, replay scope, and its policy for each state above.
* ''Owed'': the audit of each remaining contract, Cabal and Handle door against these states.

<<~/ahu>>

